  "solution": {
    "approach": "The parity of a sum depends only on the parity of its addends. If both numbers are even or both are odd, their sum is even; otherwise it is odd. Therefore for each test case we just check whether (a+b) is divisible by 2. This can be done using the modulo operator or bit‑wise AND with 1. The algorithm runs in O(T) time and O(1) extra space.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(T) – one constant‑time check per test case.",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1) – only a few variables are used irrespective of T.",
    "code": {
      "C": "",
      "C++": "",
      "Java": "import java.io.*;import java.util.*;public class Main{public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception{BufferedReader br=new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));StringTokenizer st=new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());int T=Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());StringBuilder sb=new StringBuilder();for(int i=0;i<T;i++){st=new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());long a=Long.parseLong(st.nextToken());long b=Long.parseLong(st.nextToken());sb.append(((a+b)%2==0)?\"YES\":\"NO\");if(i+1<T) sb.append('\\n');}System.out.print(sb.toString());}}",
      "Python3": "",
      "JavaScript": ""
    },
